  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_04540207790f42d2b269354f4688f493",
      "statement": "A feature vector is laid out as all trajectory floats followed by all pose floats, because the two feature section keys sit immediately after every built-in pose section and the boundary between them is the pose section's start offset.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/MmFeatureLayoutBuilder.cs#L5-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:330d7b5d33e01ce55444688175b57a1005bc1615289b869c511c1f35977131a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/MmFeatureLayout.cs#L61-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:163029ae1d9520d769aae1f7ff380253bccf546dccc06d6058a29759360c3fd2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95fc5638119d451f80f9041abebe4356",
      "statement": "A feature definition is simultaneously the authored asset data and the layout channel, and the layout keys its offset table on the descriptor's full authored content — so mutating a feature after a layout has been built makes its dictionary entry unreachable, and the layout must be rebuilt rather than the feature edited in place.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/TrajectoryFeatureChannel.cs#L10-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9593b5985de696c1e3378e81b54ea5bd5e66533bc263ef6f472b3b6a27822423:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/TrajectoryFeatureChannel.cs#L173-L205",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f30ec5f441fdc01e6cd21d810e97f8a29d8d1cebcd2a32b7be942094e5fd234:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4f3e5f0f090646d299c9354b4c43888e",
      "statement": "Inactive bone trajectory channels are switched off by zeroing their per-float weights, restored from an authored-weights snapshot when active, rather than being filled with a plausible value; filling them with the character's current bone position would score every candidate on how closely it matches the pose already playing, silently adding keep-doing-this to the objective and biasing the search against switching.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Core/MotionMatchingStage.cs#L261-L307",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af80ad210c06f92334fe00ccfffdf9a217afacc38a259e7df01f0e3bdb717423:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/CharacterController/MotionMatchingControlInput.cs#L106-L125",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fea750feaaf633817bc98ca2aeb16c60f47f9ad0381368d74d3e97df7761b1ab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ce40c249efb549bc998a2e8955817dee",
      "statement": "Simulation-frame trajectory channels are always filled and never masked; only bone channels are optional constraints, gated on the boolean return of GetBoneTrajectoryFeature whose base implementation returns false.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Core/MotionMatchingStage.cs#L261-L307",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af80ad210c06f92334fe00ccfffdf9a217afacc38a259e7df01f0e3bdb717423:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c21b4f1590ab4e8d9125724d130b3d05",
      "statement": "Because the weight array handed to the search at initialisation is the same NativeArray the query fill mutates, a per-search weight mask reaches the Burst job with no re-binding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Core/MotionMatchingStage.cs#L146-L173",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f237590e4a3426909d5539b1fb79f4c14970a5196ab48808eb5a3a439aa409c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da196d54c63c4fcb99f47edda8113615",
      "statement": "A Direction trajectory feature bakes the character's facing, not its direction of travel: for a simulation-frame channel it is the future pose's own frame forward and for a bone channel it is that bone's rest-pose forward axis, and in neither case is a position difference taken.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/TrajectoryFeatureChannel.cs#L127-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a547134f39505cf9b40819919ef215659199257829e2d68d4d82f2a54c0cb5db:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_489d2dad1f7846729a1facbafd9ae140",
      "statement": "Axis masking makes one trajectory prediction one to three floats wide, and a masked axis is not stored at all so packing and unpacking step over it; for a Direction feature the masked axes are zeroed before normalisation, so a Y-masked direction is a unit vector in the ground plane rather than the projection of a unit 3D vector.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/TrajectoryFeatureChannel.cs#L42-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d11c25a62b8e320287666864aa8448f519f8931e76a17974f776a6e1258a583:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/TrajectoryFeatureChannel.cs#L57-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6789c882f887984526e23b391023a9e77f128b7d707ea1b7c3194d071773ef9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_39bd06b2751c4424a3431dd40499b404",
      "statement": "Standard deviation is computed per feature rather than per dimension: the per-dimension deviations within one feature are averaged and that single value is written back to every float of it, so a feature's internal shape is preserved rather than each axis being independently rescaled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/FeatureSet.cs#L396-L448",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8366a30ed9227a83298dc554dddc48244d0d16031d56a2f32e3e007294f7ee3e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_02be25a0a91743c3a3ebe07a3db2a184",
      "statement": "The editor forces a simulation-frame trajectory channel to mask out Y, so such features are always two floats per prediction, because the simulation frame is a ground-plane frame.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Features/MmFeatureLayoutBuilder.cs#L5-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:330d7b5d33e01ce55444688175b57a1005bc1615289b869c511c1f35977131a6:"
